<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>
Trade-off between forget quality and model utility on LLaVA under 5% and 10% forget ratios.
The left two plots correspond to classification task, where the <math id="S4.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis shows accuracy difference on the forget set (Fgt VQA Acc Diff),
and the right two plots correspond to generation, where the <math id="S4.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis shows ROUGE-L difference on the forget set (Fgt Rouge Diff).
The <math id="S4.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-axis reports model utility on the retained (Ret) and celebrity (Cele) sets.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Ablation Study of MLLMEraser (RQ2)</h3>

